{
  "format": "kshader",
  "generator": "Kekenik Shader",
  "graph": {
    "comments": [
      {
        "color": "#60a5fa",
        "id": "note_inputs",
        "position": {
          "x": 22,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 56,
          "w": 456
        },
        "text": "UV for the grid, normal + view direction for the rim, and time."
      },
      {
        "color": "#4ade80",
        "id": "note_hex",
        "position": {
          "x": 682,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 1766
        },
        "text": "UV is offset by `scroll × time`, then the **Hexagon pattern** node returns the distance to the cell border; `1 − smoothstep(0, width, edge)` gives crisp lines."
      },
      {
        "color": "#22d3ee",
        "id": "note_rim",
        "position": {
          "x": 682,
          "y": 667
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 1154
        },
        "text": "The **Fresnel kit** lights the silhouette; a slow pulse `½ + ½ sin(t × speed)` modulates the grid so the shield breathes."
      },
      {
        "color": "#f87171",
        "id": "note_contact",
        "position": {
          "x": 2652,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 56,
          "w": 1154
        },
        "text": "The **Depth Intersection** kit measures the gap between the opaque scene behind the shield and the shield itself. `contact = (1 − fade)²` is a bright line that thins out smoothly where geometry pierces the field."
      },
      {
        "color": "#fb923c",
        "id": "note_mix",
        "position": {
          "x": 4010,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 1460
        },
        "text": "`brightness = lines × pulse + rim + opacity`; the contact line is added in its own (brighter) colour. Additive blending makes brightness the opacity."
      },
      {
        "color": "#a78bfa",
        "id": "note_out",
        "position": {
          "x": 5674,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 56,
          "w": 300
        },
        "text": "Additive, ZWrite off, two-sided — set in the graph settings."
      }
    ],
